From 50031fa1eeb4ccece48a921348475ee468072a90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rnikoopour <7692789+rnikoopour@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:38:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] lanes: a prompt pass a chunk a loop, the shortest waiting
 first (port of upstream d7b134cd, c4d07a54, 77641ba4)

A backend may give prefill_step: one chunk of the prompt pass, false while
chunks remain, Stream.fill_at its rows done. The lane host then queues an
admitted request as filling and runs one step per loop, so streams already
decoding keep their rounds during a long prompt, and picks the next step
foreground first, then fewest rows left, with a job passed over 8 times going
first. Backends without prefill_step run the pass whole, as before.

Hand-ported from ashhart/TensorFold d7b134cd, c4d07a54 and 77641ba4 (the
cherry-picks conflict with this branch's older lanes core). Tests: a stream
filled a chunk a round between another's rounds emits the whole pass's tokens
(upstream's); a short prompt sent during a long one's pass is prefilled first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
